                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1231/110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-07T16:00:00-06:00">June 7, 1934—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>81. Minister of Foreign Affairs advised me this morning that the Mexican Embassy
                    in Washington is fully prepared to discuss immediately details of a reciprocal
                    tariff agreement and that he hoped the Department would initiate negotiations at
                    an early date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
